{"name":"Churchill Downs","hex":"#a49a85","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"downs","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of down"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of down"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/downs"}],"entries":[{"title":"Churchill Downs","blocks":[{"text":"Churchill Downs is a thoroughbred horse racing complex in Louisville, Kentucky, United States. Since its opening in 1875, it has hosted the annual Kentucky Derby, the first leg of the Triple Crown, as well as the Kentucky Oaks. The venue is named after the Churchill family, prominent in Kentucky for many years. Churchill Downs has also hosted the Breeders' Cup on nine occasions, most recently on November 2 and 3, 2018."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Churchill_Downs_-_Louisville_Kentucky.jpg/330px-Churchill_Downs_-_Louisville_Kentucky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Churchill_Downs","wikidata":"Q2748049"},{"title":"Churchill Downs (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Churchill Downs\" is a song by American rapper Jack Harlow featuring Canadian rapper Drake from the former's second studio album Come Home the Kids Miss You (2022). It was produced by Boi-1da, Audi, BEDRM, and Ace G."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Churchill_Downs_(song)","wikidata":"Q112702137"},{"title":"Winston Churchill","blocks":[{"text":"Sir Winston Leonard Spencer Churchill was a British statesman, military officer, and writer who was Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 1940 to 1945, during the Second World War, and again from 1951 to 1955. For some 62 of the years between 1900 and 1964, he was a member of Parliament (MP) and represented a total of five constituencies over that time. Ideologically an adherent to economic liberalism and imperialism, he was for most of his career a member of the Conservative Party, which he led from 1940 to 1955. He was a member of the Liberal Party from 1904 to 1924."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sir_Winston_Churchill_-_19086236948_%28restored%29.jpg/330px-Sir_Winston_Churchill_-_19086236948_%28restored%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winston_Churchill","wikidata":"Q8016"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Horse_race%2C_Churchill_Downs_2008-04-18.jpg/500px-Horse_race%2C_Churchill_Downs_2008-04-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Horse_race%2C_Churchill_Downs_2008-04-18.jpg/1280px-Horse_race%2C_Churchill_Downs_2008-04-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Horse_race%2C_Churchill_Downs_2008-04-18.jpg/500px-Horse_race%2C_Churchill_Downs_2008-04-18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thoroughbreds competing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorse_race%2C_Churchill_Downs_2008-04-18.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Churchill_Downs_1901.jpg/500px-Churchill_Downs_1901.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Churchill_Downs_1901.jpg/500px-Churchill_Downs_1901.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Composite image of Churchill Downs on Derby Day, 1902","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChurchill_Downs_1901.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Stands_of_Churchill_Downs_1951.jpg/500px-Stands_of_Churchill_Downs_1951.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src"